Description: Provides tools for fitting Bayesian generalised additive
    multilevel models to time-resolved data using 'brms'. Supports
    one-dimensional time courses, cross-temporal generalisation matrices,
    and spatiotemporal measurements, including posterior summaries,
    directional evidence assessment, cluster identification, and
    visualisation of fitted effects. Designed for applications involving
    electroencephalography, magnetoencephalography, electromyography,
    pupillometry, and other time-resolved measurements. The temporal
    inference framework is described in Nalborczyk & Bürkner (2025)
    <doi:10.1101/2025.08.29.672336>.
